.TH GOLARM 1 "2026" "golarm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
golarm \- terminal clock, timer, stopwatch & alarm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B golarm
.RB [ clock ]
.RB [ \-12 ]
.RB [ \-\-fa ]
.RB [ \-\-analog [=ansi] ]
.RB [ \-\-calendar
.IR mode ]
.RB [ \-\-theme
.IR name ]
.br
.B golarm timer
.I duration
.RB [ \-l
.IR label ]
.RB [ \-q ]
.br
.B golarm chrono
.br
.B golarm alarm
.I HH:MM
.RB [ \-l
.IR label ]
.br
.B golarm
.BR \-v " | " \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B golarm
is a terminal TUI combining a live clock with a choice of calendars,
a countdown timer, a lap stopwatch, and wall-clock alarms.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B clock
Live clock (default command). Shows an optional analog dial, the Gregorian
date by default, and a day-progress bar.
.TP
.BI timer " duration"
Countdown timer.
.I duration
accepts Go syntax (\fB90s\fR, \fB5m\fR, \fB1h30m\fR), bare seconds
(\fB90\fR), and colon forms (\fB10:00\fR = mm:ss, \fB1:30:00\fR).
.TP
.B chrono
Stopwatch with lap support.
.TP
.BI alarm " HH:MM"
Alarm at a wall-clock time (24-hour, or with an am/pm suffix such as
\fB7:30pm\fR). Rolls to the next day when the time has already passed.
On fire, sends a critical desktop notification (notify-send).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-12 ", " \-\-12h
12-hour clock.
.TP
.BR \-fa ", " \-\-fa
Persian (Eastern Arabic) digits on the small text lines.
.TP
.BR \-\-analog "[=ansi]"
Open the analog clock. Golarm uses Kitty graphics when the terminal supports
them and draws the dial with color cells elsewhere. Append
.B =ansi
to force the color-cell dial.
.TP
.BI \-\-calendar " mode"
Clock date display. Choose \fBgregorian\fR (default), \fBshamsi\fR, or
\fBboth\fR. This flag overrides \fBGOLARM_CALENDAR\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Color theme: \fBdefault\fR, \fBcatppuccin\fR, \fBgruvbox\fR,
\fBtokyo-night\fR.
.TP
.BI \-l ", " \-\-label " text"
Label shown in the timer UI and its notification (timer and alarm).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Headless timer: no TUI, fire the notification and exit 0 on completion,
suitable for scripting.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GOLARM_12H=1
Default to the 12-hour clock.
.TP
.B GOLARM_FA=1
Default to Persian digits.
.TP
.B GOLARM_CALENDAR=<mode>
Default date display for the clock (\fBgregorian\fR, \fBshamsi\fR, or \fBboth\fR).
.TP
.B GOLARM_THEME=<name>
Default theme.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B space
Pause/resume; dismisses a fired timer alarm.
.TP
.B r
Restart the timer / re-arm the alarm / reset the stopwatch.
.TP
.B l
Record a lap (chrono).
.TP
.B a
Switch between analog and digital faces (clock).
.TP
.B + ", " \- ", " "left", " "right"
Adjust the remaining time by one minute (timer).
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc ", " Ctrl+C
Quit.
.SH FILES
Notifications are sent via
.BR notify-send (1).
